        "text": "Official English Q&A for BT3-040 (Mar. 28, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, since this Digimon is treated as both yellow and blue during your turn, it can digivolve into a Digimon with a requirement of \"Blue, Level 5.\"",
        "question": "Can this Digimon digivolve into a Digimon with a digivolution condition of \"Blue, Level 5\"?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't. [Your Turn] effects don't activate from breeding areas, so the card isn't treated as a yellow card. You can't digivolve it into a Digimon that requires a blue Digimon.",
        "question": "This card is in my breeding area. Can I digivolve it into a Digimon that requires a blue Digimon?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, the moment your Digimon gains a digivolution card, it no longer counts as a \"Digimon with no digivolution cards,\" and loses <Security Attack -1>.",
        "question": "My opponent has this Digimon in play. If I digivolve one of my Digimon that currently has no digivolution cards, does its <Security Attack -1> immediately disappear?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
